@startuml dict-extract-concurrency
' Why WordExtractor::add_sentence takes &self: DashMap shards the keyspace, so P
' rayon workers contend on 1/S of the map each, and the two counters are atomics.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/dict-extract-concurrency.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/dictionary/extraction.md, section "Concurrency".
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
}
title WordExtractor — shared-reference writes over a sharded map

rectangle "**rayon worker 1**\nadd_sentence(&self, s)" as w1 #546E7A
rectangle "**rayon worker 2**" as w2 #546E7A
rectangle "**rayon worker P**" as wp #546E7A

rectangle "**normalize_word**\ntrim non-alphanumeric edges · length gate\nfilter_digits · filter_special · lowercase" as nz #1565C0

rectangle "**SafeGxBuildHasher**\nh = gxhash64(w)   if |w| ≥ 16 bytes\nh = xxh3_64(w)   otherwise" as hash #1565C0

rectangle "**DashMap<String, u64>**" as dm #00838F {
  rectangle "shard 0\nRwLock<HashMap>" as s0 #00838F
  rectangle "shard 1" as s1 #00838F
  rectangle "…" as sd #00838F
  rectangle "shard S−1" as sn #00838F
}

rectangle "**AtomicU64 total_tokens**\n**AtomicUsize sentences_processed**\nfetch_add(1, Relaxed)" as at #00838F

rectangle "**entries_by_frequency() / entries_filtered(θ) / stats(θ) / to_hashmap()**\nsnapshot the map after the workers join" as out #455A64

w1 --> nz
w2 --> nz
wp --> nz
nz --> hash : Some(normalized)
nz --> out : None ⇒ token discarded,\ncounters untouched
hash --> dm : shard = h mod S
s0 -[hidden]right-> s1
s1 -[hidden]right-> sd
sd -[hidden]right-> sn
w1 --> at
w2 --> at
wp --> at
dm --> out
at --> out

note right of dm
  **Not lock-free.** The increment
  counts.entry(w).or_insert(0) += 1  takes that **one shard's** write lock. With S shards and P
  workers, the chance two workers collide on a step is ≈ 1/S
  under a uniform hash, so contention falls as S grows — but a
  hot word (Zipf's "the") still serialises on its shard.
end note

note bottom of at
  Relaxed is sound here: fetch_add is **atomic**, so the totals are
  exact. Relaxed only forgoes ordering *with respect to other data*,
  which no reader of these counters relies on.
end note

note bottom of out
  **merge(&other)** folds a second extractor in, summing per-word
  counts and both counters — so a shard-per-thread design that
  avoids the shared map entirely is a two-line change.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Role |
  |<#546E7A> | worker threads (corpus I-O) |
  |<#1565C0> | normalisation & hashing |
  |<#00838F> | shared storage |
  |<#455A64> | snapshot / results |
endlegend
@enduml
